.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:3:description: Executor edited the main-tree file instead of the worktree copy when constructing absolute paths without the worktree-root prefix.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:9:session: 45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:10:tags: [process, worktree, execution]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:21:During T07 iter2, the executor needed to edit `.codex/AGENTS.md`. The worktree is at `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9/`. The worktree copy of `.codex/AGENTS.md` lives at:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:23:`/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9/.codex/AGENTS.md`
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:29:The executor initially ran the Edit tool against the main-tree absolute path (`/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.codex/AGENTS.md`) instead of the worktree-physical copy. The error was caught (the Edit succeeded against the main tree, which was the wrong target). The executor then restored the main-tree file to its prior state and re-applied the edit against the correct worktree path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:33:The executor resolved the path from the filename `.codex/AGENTS.md` without verifying that the path was under the worktree root. The cwd for Bash calls is the worktree root, but the Edit tool accepts absolute paths — so a relative conceptualization (`just .codex/AGENTS.md`) silently resolves to the main-tree absolute path rather than the worktree-physical path. The worktree-physical path requires the full prefix `/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:37:Before any Edit in a worktree session:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:38:1. Confirm `pwd` = worktree root (or run `pwd` in Bash to verify).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:39:2. For every file to be edited, verify the absolute path begins with the worktree root prefix, not the repo root.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:40:3. When constructing the target path, always prepend `<worktree-root>/` explicitly — never infer from a short relative filename.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:45:- You are working in a worktree session and need to edit a file that also exists in the main tree (e.g., `.codex/AGENTS.md`, `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/...`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:46:- You construct an absolute path that starts at the repo root (`/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/`) rather than the worktree root (`/playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/session-2026-05-24-45388fa9/`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:47:- The Edit tool succeeds — no error is thrown — but git diff in the worktree shows no changes, while `git diff` in the main tree shows the change. This is the hallmark of the wrong-target edit.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:51:- [[executor-mirror-path-vs-worktree-physical-copy]] — same class: a file that exists in both the main tree and the worktree resolves to the main tree when referenced without the explicit worktree-root prefix.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/executor-main-tree-edit-near-miss.md:52:- `mistakes/codex-wrapper-relative-path-wrong-session-write.md` — same class: path resolves to wrong location when worktree prefix is omitted
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:9:session: a10c82d6-f4c4-4ee5-a3dc-9fb7ce3815e7
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:27:- Therefore editing the canonical `.gobbi/.../skills/X/SKILL.md` is reflected in `.claude/skills/X/SKILL.md` automatically — **one edit, not two**.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:33:The leader conflated two separate facts from mistake `executor-mirror-path-vs-worktree-physical-copy.md`:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:35:1. (TRUE) The `.gobbi/.../skills/` real files are branch-isolated — each worktree has its own copy on its branch, so a worktree executor must edit the worktree-absolute `.gobbi/...` path, not the main tree's.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:38:The existing mistake's wording ("physical copies on the branch, not symlinks back to the main tree") is about worktree-isolation of the *canonical real files*; it is easily misread as "the mirror doubles edits." A clarification / cross-link to this mistake is a deferred follow-up.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:42:- Edit the **canonical** file at `<worktree>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/{skill}/...` (worktree-absolute). The `.claude/skills/{skill}/...` symlink reflects it automatically — do NOT make a second edit.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:44:- Verify with `readlink .claude/skills/{skill}/SKILL.md` and `find .claude/skills -type l | wc -l`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:50:- A P13 CRUD plan listing `.claude/skills/X/SKILL.md` as a separate Update line from `.gobbi/.../skills/X/SKILL.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:54:- `mistakes/executor-mirror-path-vs-worktree-physical-copy.md` — the misread source; its real lesson is worktree branch-isolation (canonical files are worktree-local), NOT that the `.claude↔.gobbi` mirror doubles edits. Deferred follow-up: clarify/cross-link in W5-T2.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/skills-mirror-symlinks-not-copies.md:56:- Session: 2026-05-25-a10c82d6 ideation, staging decision `skills-mirror-is-symlinks-not-physical-copies.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:3:description: A SendMessage-continued executor's Bash shell cwd resets to the session default (main tree root) — a "cwd still X" prose statement does not substitute for an explicit cd; the continued agent edited and committed in the wrong tree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:9:session: a10c82d6-f4c4-4ee5-a3dc-9fb7ce3815e7
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:10:tags: [process, worktree, sendmessage, cwd-reset, git]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:21:Wave 1 iter2 remediation was delegated via `SendMessage` to continue the W1 executor. The continuation prompt said "cwd still `<worktree>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi`" rather than re-issuing an explicit `cd <worktree>` as the first action. The continued agent's shell cwd had reset to the session default (the MAIN TREE root), it did not re-cd, and it edited + committed `75dbaad` (the `feature: null` fix) onto the **main tree's `develop` branch** instead of the worktree branch `chore/session-2026-05-25-a10c82d6`. Detected by the manager's independent post-eval grep: the worktree file still showed `feature: project-memory` and the commit was absent from the worktree branch range, while local `develop` was 1 commit ahead of `origin/develop`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:25:The manager assumed a `SendMessage`-continued subagent retains the shell cwd from its prior turn. It does not — each subagent turn's Bash cwd resets to the session start directory (the main tree), exactly as documented for the manager's own Bash calls (`codex/SKILL.md` § CWD inheritance). The "cwd still ..." phrasing is a statement, not an action; the agent never ran `cd`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:29:1. EVERY delegation prompt — including `SendMessage` continuations — MUST make `cd <worktree-absolute-path>` the explicit FIRST ACTION, never "cwd is still X". Re-state the absolute worktree path each time.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:30:2. Manager MUST run an independent post-WORK verification in the worktree (grep the actual file at the worktree-absolute path + confirm the commit is in `git log <worktree-branch>`), not trust the producer's reported SHA — this is what caught it.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:31:3. Recovery when it happens: do NOT cherry-pick blindly (the main-tree file may be a stale pre-migration version causing conflicts); re-make the edit directly in the worktree and commit there; then clean the misplaced commit off the integration branch (safe if not yet pushed to origin).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:35:- Any remediation/continuation delegation (`SendMessage`) to an executor or evaluator that will run `git`/Edit in a worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:36:- Symptom after the fact: the producer reports a commit SHA + verify-pass, but the manager's independent check in the worktree shows the change absent and the commit on a different branch (often `develop` = main tree HEAD).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:41:- [[executor-mirror-path-vs-worktree-physical-copy]] — broader class: worktree-vs-main-tree path confusion.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:42:- [[manager-skipped-dual-system-eval]] — the independent manager verify (post-WORK grep) that caught this is the same discipline mandated there.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/sendmessage-continued-cwd-resets-to-main-tree.md:43:- `sessions/2026-05-25-a10c82d6-f4c4-4ee5-a3dc-9fb7ce3815e7/execution/w1/staging/decisions/sendmessage-continued-executor-edits-main-tree.md` — originating staged candidate.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:9:session: 7ea62d36-e826-4ce6-9e90-9e948007b068
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:10:tags: [process, codex, evaluation, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:21:During Ideation iter3 evaluation, the manager dispatched a `codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent to perform the Codex evaluation of `draft-iter3.md`. The agent returned quickly with a placeholder message indicating the task was still running. No evaluation files were written to the session staging directory. The evaluation directory `evaluation/iter3/codex/` remained empty. The manager had to authorize recovery via direct `codex exec` from a Bash tool call, which succeeded synchronously and produced all 8 evaluation files.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:23:The `codex:codex-rescue` plugin agent fires the codex companion task asynchronously and returns immediately, without awaiting completion or capturing real output. Its response is a placeholder like "task is still running" or "the background job has been submitted". The underlying `codex-companion.mjs` tracks jobs in `broker.json` (e.g., `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/.../state.json`) with a `status` field. The plugin agent does not poll for `status="completed"` before returning — it delegates to the runtime and exits.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:27:The manager assumed `codex:codex-rescue` behaves synchronously: spawn, wait for completion, read output. In reality the plugin agent's "job is to forward the request to the Codex companion script" (per `agents/codex-rescue.md:12`) and return. The forwarding is asynchronous. The manager did not check whether the codex:codex-rescue agent contract guarantees synchronous completion. Result: zero files written, evaluation directory empty, session blocked.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:31:1. **Use `codex exec` via Bash directly (synchronous, universal pattern)**. Replace `Agent(subagent_type="codex:codex-rescue", ...)` with a direct Bash invocation:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:41:   find /playinganalytics/git/gobbi/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/{session-id}/{loop}/evaluation/iter{n}/codex/ -name '*.md'
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:43:   Confirm files exist at the main-tree absolute path (not nested in any worktree). This is the 3rd corrective from `mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:45:3. **Manager-side `codex:codex-rescue` usage**. If the plugin agent is used (manager-only convenience), the manager must monitor the background job to completion — poll `/codex:status` (user-only) or check broker.json status — before treating the output as available. This is not scalable for evaluation flows; prefer `codex exec` directly.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:51:- The targeted output directory (e.g., `evaluation/iter3/codex/`) remains empty after the agent returns.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:53:- No `.md` files appear under `sessions/{session-id}/{loop}/evaluation/iter{n}/codex/` after the spawn.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:57:- `mistakes/codex-eval-session-write-path-nested-in-worktree.md` — companion mistake (wrong write path when worktree CWD is inherited)
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:58:- Design A of this session: codex skill invocation-patterns section, "Why subagents must use `codex exec`"
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/codex-rescue-agent-fire-and-forget-without-result-capture.md:61:- Empirical witness: iter3 Codex evaluation was initially unavailable because `codex:codex-rescue` returned a placeholder; direct `codex exec` succeeded and produced all 8 evaluation files within the session
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:2:name: session-dir-placed-outside-worktree
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:3:description: Manager bootstrap placed the session directory at the main-tree path instead of inside the worktree in worktree-pr mode.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:9:session: 45388fa9-74a5-42ff-acdf-1308ca35523f
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:10:tags: [session-lifecycle, worktree, bootstrap, orchestration]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:17:# Manager bootstrap placed session dir outside the worktree in worktree-pr mode
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:21:During Configuration Step 1 rows 5 and 6, the manager wrote `state.json`, `settings.json`, and `session.json` to the **main-tree absolute path** (`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/2026-05-24-45388fa9-.../`). The session was running in `worktree-pr` mode with `session.json.git.worktreePath` already resolved to the worktree root. Subsequent Ideation iter1/iter2 leader artifacts and the iter2 dual-system evaluation artifacts inherited the wrong location, all landing under the main-tree session dir rather than inside the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:23:The user flagged it after the dual-system evaluators were dispatched. The manager had to move the entire session directory tree from the main-tree path into the worktree.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:27:The user explicitly flagged the misplacement after evaluator outputs landed in the wrong location. The correction was: move the session directory tree from the main-tree `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` path into `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` before continuing.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:31:The orchestration skill's Configuration Step 1 procedure (rows 5 and 6) specifies the session-file path as `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/...` — a **relative** path with no explicit tree qualifier. The manager resolved the relative path against the current working directory (the main tree, where the session started), not against `session.json.git.worktreePath`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:33:The qualified absolute-root rule lives in `git/SKILL.md` § Memory Access Matrix (`**Critical rule — write paths**` at line 33) and bundle-B design doc `qualified-git-write-path-rule.md`. The manager either failed to load that rule before bootstrap, or loaded it but did not apply it to Configuration rows 5 and 6 because the orchestration rows themselves do not cite the qualifier inline.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:35:A compounding factor: prior sessions used `worktreePath: null` (direct mode), so every session a fresh manager could inspect for the convention was a direct-mode session where main-tree placement was correct. The divergence only surfaces in `worktree-pr` mode.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:37:The row-ordering tension makes this structurally fragile: row 5 (state.json) fires before row 5.5 (worktree create), so the worktree doesn't exist when row 5 resolves the write path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:43:1. Check `settings.git.workflow.mode`. If `worktree-pr`, compute the absolute write-root: `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/{date}-{session-id}/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:44:2. Reorder row 5.5 (worktree create) to **before** row 5 so `worktreePath` is known when row 5 writes state.json.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:45:3. Row 5 path-resolution: if `worktreePath` is set, write to `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/...`; if null (direct mode), write to main-tree `.gobbi/...`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:48:For immediate remediation when this is caught mid-session: move the entire session directory tree from the main-tree path into the worktree path using `mv`. Since `.gobbi/projects/` is whitelisted in the repo's gitignore (`!.gobbi/projects/`), the moved dir at the worktree path will be a tracked path that `git -C "$worktreePath" add` can include.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:50:The orchestration skill text (rows 5 and 6) must cite the qualified absolute-root rule inline with a direct pointer to `git/SKILL.md` § Memory Access Matrix and to `qualified-git-write-path-rule.md`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:56:- You are in `worktree-pr` mode and about to run Configuration Step 1 rows 5–6.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:57:- The orchestration skill's row 5 says "write `.gobbi/projects/{project-name}/sessions/…`" without a tree qualifier.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:58:- `session.json.git.worktreePath` is already resolved but the row doesn't reference it for the write path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:60:If after Configuration you notice that session artifacts (state.json, session.json, evaluation outputs) are appearing at `<main-tree>/.gobbi/projects/gobbi/sessions/…` rather than `<worktreePath>/.gobbi/…`, the misplacement has occurred and needs immediate remediation (mv + re-commit).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:64:- `codex-subprocess-writes-to-main-tree.md` — the session that surfaced this mistake also saw evaluator subagents (both Claude and Codex legs) write EVAL artifacts to the main tree; same root cause (CWD defaults to main tree, path macros aren't resolved by subagents).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/session-dir-placed-outside-worktree.md:66:- `per-iteration-session-commit-cadence.md` — `git -C "$worktreePath" add` cannot see session memory placed outside the worktree; this mistake silently breaks the per-iter commit cadence.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:9:session: 5786090e-f65a-4493-94cc-e610ce337813
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:10:tags: [process, evaluation, dual-system, prose-wave, template-conformance]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:17:# Dual-system evaluation: Codex caught template-form gaps that Claude and the executor missed
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:27:1. **F1 — cross-feature ref wrongly removed.** The executor deleted a `Related` link to `features/install-runtime/references/claude-code-transcript-tooluseresult-empirical.md`. The target exists in the project tree. The ref was a cross-feature empirical link, not a sibling-feature link — both the executor and Claude's evaluator only checked the sibling (`features/guardrails/`) scope for cross-ref validity. Codex resolved the path in the wider project tree and caught the broken pointer.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:33:4. **F4 — backlogs missing concrete session path.** Two backlogs' Originating-session field carried a freeform label instead of the canonical `sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-{id}/` path. Claude's evaluator accepted the label as present; Codex checked the field's format against the template contract and flagged the missing path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:39:- **Cross-feature scope blindness.** The executor and Claude both scoped cross-ref verification to the immediate sibling directory. Cross-feature refs require resolving the path in the entire project tree (`features/*/references/`), not just `features/{current}/`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:41:- **Missing structural diffs.** README Subdirectories and backlog Originating-session fields both require diffing against a live ground truth (`ls -d */` and the session-path pattern, respectively). Neither diff was run in iter1.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:45:- An evaluator PASS that does NOT explicitly confirm: (a) cross-feature ref targets exist (not just sibling-dir refs); (b) checklist headings match one of the template's exact named forms; (c) README Subdirectories list was diffed against `ls -d */`; (d) backlog Originating-session carries the canonical `sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-{id}/` path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:56:4. **Backlog session-path format**: the Originating-session field must contain `sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-{id}/` (or a session anchor resolvable to a sessions/ directory). A freeform label is insufficient.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:58:Dual-system evaluation is mandatory precisely because Claude and Codex catch different classes of defect. Manager must ground-truth all divergences before iter2 is authorized.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:62:- [[evaluator-false-pass-without-diffing]] — the parent mistake this extends
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/dual-system-codex-caught-template-form-gaps-claude-missed.md:63:- `execution/P4-guardrails-prose/artifacts/verification-report.md` — the session evidence for this mistake
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:2:name: worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:4:type: mistakes
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:5:scope: project
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:9:session: 1b26cf20-677b-498c-8c1b-7d7e971597ac
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:10:tags: [process, worktree, execution]
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:20:During a dispatch into the worktree at `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/worktrees/chore/268-session-foundations-bundle-b/`, the manager observed that 953 files showed in `git status --short` as ` D` (working-tree deleted, index retained). The Edit and Read tools failed against those paths because the physical files were missing, yet `git -C <worktree> show HEAD:<path>` succeeded — proving the tracked version existed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:22:The corrective stance: adopt a pre-flight worktree-integrity check before any executor or assistant editing pass against the worktree:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:25:PHYS=$(git -C <worktree> status --short | grep -c "^ D")
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:27:  git -C <worktree> checkout HEAD -- .
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:35:- Failing Read/Edit calls inside an executor produce confusing errors that look like missing files rather than worktree-state drift, so the executor mis-diagnoses the problem.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:40:- Recreate the worktree from scratch. Rejected — destroys per-iter commits that may not be pushed.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:41:- Trust the executor to detect the missing files. Rejected — Read tool failures look like missing-file errors, not worktree drift.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:45:- Delegation prompts targeting worktree files should include the pre-flight check or a "restore-if-needed" note.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:46:- Wrap-up's own routing pass may need to run the same pre-flight if it ever writes to worktree-internal paths (currently it writes only to main-tree `.gobbi/projects/gobbi/` so does not).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:50:- Pre-flight: `git -C <worktree> status --short | grep -c "^ D"` — if > 0, run `git -C <worktree> checkout HEAD -- <path>`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:55:- Bash `ls <worktree>/.gobbi/projects/...` returns "No such file or directory" but `git -C <worktree> ls-files <path>` returns the path.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:56:- `git -C <worktree> status --short | head` shows many ` D` (space-D) entries.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/mistakes/worktree-physical-file-missing-when-checked-out.md:59:- T1 implementation (PR #269) — worktree-first session architecture
