.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:234:### Inter-loop transition
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:238:| Chat | AskUserQuestion to confirm advance to step `N+1`; user may revise scope, abort, or branch |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:239:| Auto | Auto-advance to step `N+1`. Halt only if a `maxIterations` abort makes downstream infeasible or a user-authority decision is required |
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:241:In both modes, the manager NEVER skips `EVALUATION` (unless `evaluate.mode == 'skip'`) or `MEMORIZATION`. Mode controls user gates; it does not relax the workflow.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:245:## Workflow Status Display
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:247:In both modes, the manager renders a workflow status snapshot so the user can see, at a glance, where the session is. The display is a projection of the session's `state.json` (see [Workflow State Machine § State persistence](#state-persistence) for where it lives and how it is updated). The snapshot is shown before every AskUserQuestion in Chat Mode, at every loop boundary in Auto Mode, and any time the user asks for status.
