.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:366:`iter` starts at `0` on loop entry. `maxIterations` is read from `workflow.{step}.maxIterations` (default `3`).
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:368:If `evaluate.mode == 'skip'`, the loop bypasses `EVALUATION` and proceeds `WORK` → `MEMORIZATION` → `ITER / EXIT` on the first pass; the absent verdict is treated as `Skipped` at `ITER / EXIT`.
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:380:After `EVALUATION` (or its skip path), the loop always proceeds to `MEMORIZATION`. The iteration decision happens at `ITER / EXIT`:
.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/orchestration/SKILL.md:383:- **`Skipped`** (no verdict because `evaluate.mode == 'skip'`) → exit the loop. Surface the work artifact.
